Fillets: an analytic blend split into its faces' domains keeps all its
pieces at the spine's last end where none of them runs into a face at the
end, as it does at the first end (mitcad#1349).

SplitKPart keeps, at an end of the spine, the pieces up to the one whose
contact runs into a face at the end. At the first end, where no piece does,
it kept them all; at the last end it removed them all, and the edge's blend
was walked instead (patch 0970 kept them at the last end only where the end
is at a wall's corner tighter than the ball). A fin's top rounded along its
last arc up to the fin's end face, which goes on from the arc's top
tangentially: the arc's torus reaches the end face only past the spine's
end, which ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd then cuts (patch 1310). On one side of the
fin the spine ends there and the torus was dropped and walked, a B-spline
face where the stored body has the torus, and 1350's transition before it
could not run it on. The last end now keeps them all as the first does.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_top_creases.cpp,
test_transitions_cut_by_their_pieces (with 1350 and 1352).

Upstream: new.

